      "immutable": false,
      "summary": "Pin the 50 revision pairs of the R01-R50 brief",
      "body": "Setup for llm-dlc/loops/organic-java-merged-pr-links-r01-r50-brief.md, no claims. Fetched the 100 pinned commits (and the two middle commits of the two-commit ranges R24 and R50) into shallow mirrors under ~/.cache/in-the-loop/git-mirrors, created one worktree per revision in ~/.cache/in-the-loop/merged-pr-links-r01-r50, and checked with gh api that every PR is merged, its merge commit is the brief's after revision, the after revision's first parent is the before revision (R24 and R50 apart, as the brief says), and the landed diff names exactly the PR's files. Builds and landed-test checks follow.",
      "log_sha256": "d2ef6d35e3c10530a3a37ab97c3e131b15fe0bc098da80527effdb4e07f74edf"
    },
    {
      "change_id": "loxnmknutyywpwpvwuvomuomyxllznvs",
      "commit_id": null,
      "immutable": false,
      "summary": "Record the R01-R50 setup of 13 small Maven cases",
      "body": "Setup for llm-dlc/loops/organic-java-merged-pr-links-r01-r50-brief.md, no claims. Built both pins of R02, R06, R11, R12, R13, R15, R16, R17, R20, R21, R22, R26 and R40 with Maven (online, then offline), kept the jars, class digests and classpaths, and ran each PR's landed tests: they pass on the fix, the parent's own copies pass on the parent, and the fix's tests fail on the parent as the brief says. Release sides were compared with each pin and their checksums and signatures checked. R16 builds against a commons-io 2.21.0-SNAPSHOT that is gone, rebuilt from its public source and recorded as a substitute.",
      "log_sha256": "0c125b2e37f0d09b436334cb95a07fab591bb9c93c9ba3f38c5a43b02cd06b87"
    },
    {
      "change_id": "wslqrlnzxlsoxmryoromkqvmltkvtvvo",
      "commit_id": null,
      "immutable": false,
      "summary": "Record the R01-R50 setup of 13 medium Maven cases",
      "body": "Setup for llm-dlc/loops/organic-java-merged-pr-links-r01-r50-brief.md, no claims. Built both pins of R03, R07, R08, R10, R18, R19, R23, R24, R27, R28, R29, R30 and R48 with Maven (online, then offline), kept jars, class digests and classpaths, and ran each PR's landed tests inline: they pass on the fix and the fix's tests fail on the parent as the PRs say. R18's gone jackson-base snapshot parent was rebuilt from public jackson-bom source; R28-R30 resolved later snapshot builds of their Jackson 3 dependencies than the pins used, recorded with digests and saved copies. Release sides compared and their checksums and signatures checked.",
      "log_sha256": "d24870c6966c64c8a5024003d71b1b4d9fb98af1fec9165d26e9b7435a04f761"
